Translate Contoso's ServiceNow business rules into instances of Contoso's model (LinkML;
the JSON Schema you must answer in is generated from it). Each rule that decides who must approve a data access
request becomes one ContosoApprovalRule:
- approver_kind dataset_owner when the dataset's owner approves; role when anyone with approver_role approves.
- approver_role is a role id from: [{"id": "access-administrator", "name": "Access administrator"}, {"id": "access-fulfilment-agent", "name": "Access fulfilment agent"}, {"id": "contract-analyst", "name": "Contract analyst"}, {"id": "credit-analyst", "name": "Credit analyst"}, {"id": "data-engineer", "name": "Data engineer"}, {"id": "data-owner", "name": "Data owner"}, {"id": "finance-controller", "name": "Finance controller"}, {"id": "quantitative-researcher", "name": "Quantitative researcher"}, {"id": "security-analyst", "name": "Security analyst"}]
- min_classification and domain narrow which datasets it applies to (classification order: public < internal <
  confidential < restricted). Datasets: [{"id": "loan_book", "classification": "confidential", "domain": "credit", "owner": "yusuf.garcia"}, {"id": "credit_risk_mart", "classification": "confidential", "domain": "credit", "owner": "yusuf.garcia"}, {"id": "counterparty_exposure", "classification": "restricted", "domain": "credit", "owner": "yusuf.garcia"}, {"id": "market_data_eod", "classification": "internal", "domain": "markets", "owner": "grace.iyer"}, {"id": "trade_blotter", "classification": "confidential", "domain": "markets", "owner": "grace.iyer"}, {"id": "research_notes", "classification": "internal", "domain": "markets", "owner": "grace.iyer"}, {"id": "fx_rates", "classification": "public", "domain": "markets", "owner": "grace.iyer"}, {"id": "esg_scores", "classification": "public", "domain": "markets", "owner": "grace.iyer"}, {"id": "gl_actuals", "classification": "restricted", "domain": "finance", "owner": "zane.silva"}, {"id": "budget_forecast", "classification": "confidential", "domain": "finance", "owner": "zane.silva"}, {"id": "client_master", "classification": "restricted", "domain": "operations", "owner": "yara.novak"}, {"id": "payroll", "classification": "restricted", "domain": "hr", "owner": "zane.moreau"}]
- year_end_close_days, if the rule only applies in the days before the financial year end (31 March).
For rules that decide something other than approval (for example a required field), set approval_rule to null in
source_rules and say in the note which vocabulary term already expresses it.
